{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_parts_of_the_law", "label": "The parts of the law (at least three, count stated as a floor)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/PARTS-OF-THE-LAW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The three parts are distinguished by WHAT FALSIFIES each, which is the only distinction that survives a rewrite; the count is a floor, and the possible merge of parts 2 and 3 is stated alongside it rather than resolved by preference."}, {"id": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_part_1_ordering", "label": "Part 1 - the ordering (which channel the entrant takes)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PARTS-OF-THE-LAW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_part_2_promotion", "label": "Part 2 - the promotion (the single d-1 s+1 defect)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PARTS-OF-THE-LAW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every one of the eight failures is the same defect d-1 s+1 (magnitude 1, except Pd where it is 2); no operator exists, and a one-electron-at-a-time walk cannot express it and does not attempt to."}, {"id": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_part_3_openings", "label": "Part 3 - the openings (La opens 5d, Ac opens 6d)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PARTS-OF-THE-LAW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At La the rule names the WRONG CHANNEL, so part 1 is what fails and cannot absorb it, and no already-placed electron moves, so part 2 cannot either - which is why part 3 is not a subcase of either."}, {"id": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_orbital_collapse_candidate", "label": "Orbital collapse: the Janet boundary is not sharp", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PARTS-OF-THE-LAW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Collapse is rapid, not instantaneous (Ba II nf = 0.756 against a threshold of 57; Ca I nd = 0.908 against 21), sourced to Goeppert-Mayer 1941 and Griffin-Andrew-Cowan 1969; it is already in the chain and is not imported for this, and it is the CANDIDATE, not the mechanism."}, {"id": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_derived_not_fitted", "label": "Derived, not fitted (no constant beyond c = 137.035999)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PARTS-OF-THE-LAW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A correction applied at 57 and 89 because that is where the rule breaks would be an empirical input and is forbidden; the collapse route is admissible precisely because it predicts where the threshold falls rather than being placed at it."}, {"id": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_prediction_openings", "label": "PREDICTION-OPENINGS filed before Z=57 runs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PARTS-OF-THE-LAW.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "La and Ac are the only two elements where the step column can fail for a reason that is not a promotion, so the prediction must be written before nlchain is pointed at Z=57 and again before Z=89 - the sharpest single test the walk contains."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_parts_of_the_law", "target": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_part_1_ordering", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/PARTS-OF-THE-LAW.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_parts_of_the_law", "target": "recovered_parts_of_the_law_part_2_promotion", "relation": "references", 